## 4. Modification

You are permitted to modify the Software for non-commercial purposes.

If You distribute a modified version, You must:

1. retain this License;
2. retain applicable copyright and attribution notices;
3. clearly indicate that modifications were made;
4. identify the modified version as being derived from MiraiLens; and
5. not represent the modified version as the official MiraiLens release.

Modified versions must not falsely imply endorsement, sponsorship, or
official affiliation with MiraiLens.

---

## 5. Attribution

When distributing a modified version of MiraiLens, You must provide
reasonable attribution to the original project.

The attribution should identify:

**MiraiLens — developed by Sachin Patel**

and include a link to the official MiraiLens project repository where
reasonably practical.

Example:

> Based on MiraiLens by Sachin Patel  
> https://github.com/mugenkyou/mcp-server-mirailens

You may additionally identify your own modifications and contributors.

Nothing in this section prevents You from accurately identifying the
authors of your own original contributions.

